  "strategy": "**Approach and Rationale**  \nThe current algorithm relies on multi-resolution optimization and local searches with SLSQP, but it may get stuck in local optima due to insufficient exploration. This material change introduces Bayesian optimization with dimensionality reduction via fast Fourier transforms (FFT) to efficiently explore global optima. The solution:  \n1. **Analysis via FFT**: Transform the problem into the frequency domain to identify periodic components and their interactions.  \n2. **Bayesian Optimization**: Global exploration guided by a probabilistic model, contrasting with local SLSQP refinement.  \n3. **Frequency-domain Shape Synthesis**: Generate candidate solutions from optimized Fourier modes, ensuring diversity and feasibility.  \n4. **Hierarchical Search**: Operates at multiple scales (from coarse to fine frequency grids) to transition smoothly between resolutions.  \nThis approach explicitly connects signal structure to the overlap integral, leveraging mathematical physics principles to avoid local minima.  \n\n**Mathematical Specification**  \nThe objective is:  \n\\[ C_5 = \\max_{k} \\int h(x)[1 - h(x+k)] \\, dx \\]  \nsubject to:  \n1. \\( 0 \\le h(x) \\le 1 \\),  \n2. \\(\\int_0^2 h(x) \\, dx = 1\\),  \n3. \\(h(x)\\) periodic with period 2 (or anti-periodic if needed).  \n\n**Implementation Procedure**  \n1. **Initial Setup**:  \n   - Read `initial_h_values` (if provided) and `budget_s`.  \n   - Define resolutions per frequency grid: `freq_grids = [[0.1, 0.2, ..., 5], [5, 10, ..., 50], [50, 100, ..., 500]]`  \n   - Set hyperparameters: alpha schedule, random seed, and budget thresholds.  \n\n2. **Bayesian Optimization Loop**:  \n   a. **Phase 1: High-Level Synthesis**  \n      i. Discretize frequency space using FFT.  \n      ii. Generate candidate Fourier spectra \\(S(\\omega)\\) satisfying \\(\\sum \\omega^2 |S(\\omega)|^2 < \\infty\\).  \n      iii. Project to unconstrained optimization variables.  \n      iv. Compute likelihood:  \n         \\[\n         L(\\theta) = -\\left( \\max_k C_5(\\hat{h}) - \\epsilon k \\right)\n         \\]  \n      v. Use Gaussian process regression to learn surrogate model.  \n   b. **Phase 2: Refinement**  \n      i. For optimal frequency grid \\(\\omega^*, \\theta^*\\):  \n         - Upsample via inverse FFT and apply feasibility projection:  \n           \\[\n           h = \\Pi_{[0,1]} \\circ \\text{IFFT}(S^*(\\omega)) + \\delta \\cdot \\text{threshold}\n           \\]  \n         - Use SLSQP for fine tuning.  \n   c. **Constraint Enforcement**:  \n      - Post-projection: clip values and adjust sum.  \n      - Feasibility map: repair infeasible projections via:  \n        \\[\n        \\text{clip}(h) \\to g(h) = \\arg\\min_{\\tilde{h}} \\|\\tilde{h} - h\\|_{\\text{TV}}, \\quad \\int g(h) = 0.5\n        \\]  \n\n3. **Time Budget**  \n   - Allocate 40%: Phase 1 setup  \n   - 20%: Bayesian acquisition  \n   - 30%: SLSQP polishing  \n   - 10%: Diverted to frequency density analysis  \n\n**Search Choices**  \n- **Frequency Priors**: Use Sobol sequence for initialization.  \n- **Acquisition Function**: Expected Improvement (EI) with noise tolerance.  \n- **Ensemble Size**: 5 models in the Bayesian hierarchy.  \n- **Fallback**: Retain `initial_h_values` if Bayesian plateau occurs.  \n\n**Compute Budget & Robustness**  \n- **Complexity**: \\(O(\\#\\text{freq} \\cdot |\\text{budget}|)\\) per run.  \n- **Checkpoints**: Restart acquisition if worst-case time exceeds 60%.  \n- **Fallback Logic**  \n   a. Snap to nearest projection:  \n      \\[\n      h_{\\text{def}} = \\text{project}_N(\\text{nearest\\_neighbor}(h_{\\text{current}}))\n      \\]  \n   b. Interpolate previous best if feasible.  \n   c. Final pass with alpha=1000.  \n\n**Validation and Return Contract**  \n1. **Sanity Checks**:  \n   a. \\(\\text{np.all}(0.0 \\le h_{\\text{out}} \\le 1.0)\\)  \n   b. \\(\\left|\\int h_{\\text{out}} \\, dx - 1 \\right| / \\text{budget} \\le 1e-5\\)  \n   c. `c5_bound = compute_c5(h_out, n_points) < 0.3809`  \n2. **Re-evaluation**: Compute objective with tolerance \\(1e-6\\).  \n3. **Output Formatting**  \n   \\[\n   (\\text{np.clip}(h, 0, 1), \\text{c5_bound}, \\text{n_points})\n   \\]  \n\n**Implementation Details**  \nHelpers must:  \n- `gen_freq_samples(n, alpha)`: Generate spectral candidates via inverse FFT.  \n- `fft_to_func(h_in)`: Convert Fourier-transformed samples to grid function.  \n- `project_fft(h_in, target_sum)`: Enforce integral constraint via optimization.  \n\nCode template:  \n```python\ndef objective_bayes(theta, alpha):  # Transform theta to h, compute C_5 via FFT\ndef grad_objective_bayes(theta, alpha):  # FFT-based gradient?\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize from skopt import gp_minimize\ngp = GaussianProcessRegressor()  # Surrogate model for EI acquisition\n```  \n\nBayesian phases operate in **log-frequency space** to avoid grid bias.",
